   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "One way to solve this problem is to appeal to geometric facts related to vision and this is the approach taken by Descartes and Malebranche among others. If both eyes fixate on an object at a moderate distance, then the angle defined by the optic axes of the two eyes will specify the distance of that object (given the distance between the eyes). The closer to parallel the optic axes of the two eyes are, the further away the object is. Visual perception of distance relies, according to this propo",
   "md_text": "One way to solve this problem is to appeal to geometric facts related to vision and this is the approach taken by Descartes and Malebranche among others. If both eyes fixate on an object at a moderate distance, then the angle defined by the optic axes of the two eyes will specify the distance of that object (given the distance between the eyes). The closer to parallel the optic axes of the two eyes are, the further away the object is. Visual perception of distance relies, according to this propo"
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "shape_h": "ol",
   "shape_m": "ol",
   "html_text": "We perceive ordinary objects (houses, mountains, etc.). We perceive only ideas.",
